certutil -store My 
Opens and displays the certificates stored in the current user's or computer's **"Personal" (My)** certificate store, which typically contains personal certificates used for client authentication, code signing, or encryption.

certutil -store Root 
Displays the certificates in the **Trusted Root Certification Authorities** store, listing the trusted root certificates that the operating system uses to verify the authenticity of other certificates.

certutil -verify -urlfetch C:\temp\cert.cer
Validates a specific certificate file (`cert.cer`) against its issuing Certificate Authority, automatically fetching and checking Certificate Revocation Lists (CRLs) and AIA (Authority Information Access) URLs referenced inside the certificate to ensure it hasn't been revoked.

certutil -hashfile C:\temp\file.iso SHA256
Generates and displays the cryptographic hash (using the **SHA256** algorithm) of a specified file (`file.iso`), commonly used to verify file integrity and check that a download hasn't been corrupted or tampered with.

Get-ChildItem Cert:\LocalMachine\My | Select-Object Subject, NotAfter
A PowerShell command that queries the local machine's personal certificate store (`Cert:\LocalMachine\My`) and filters the output to display only the **Subject** (who the certificate belongs to) and the **NotAfter** expiration date for each certificate.

